sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: A first protected request
    accDescr: Three phases. The Workload's CONNECT waits while the user approves a certificate in the Companion. The Gateway then verifies the site and gets the TLS handshake signed on the desktop through the Broker. Finally the request and response flow through the Gateway.
    participant W as Workload
    participant G as Gateway
    participant B as Broker
    participant C as Companion
    participant S as Site
    rect {band-request}
    Note over W,S: Request and approval
    W->>G: CONNECT
    G->>B: Bind job and host
    B-->>C: Notify with ID
    C->>B: Fetch offer
    Note over C: User picks a certificate and duration
    C->>B: Approve, send chain
    B->>C: Activate grant
    C-->>B: Ready
    end
    rect {band-sign}
    Note over W,S: Upstream handshake, signed on the desktop
    G->>B: Look up grant and acquire leases
    G->>S: Begin upstream TLS
    S-->>G: Server proof and client certificate request
    Note over G: Verify server
    G->>B: Request signature
    B->>C: Sign handshake
    C-->>B: Native signature
    B-->>G: Verified signature
    end
    rect {band-request}
    Note over W,S: Application traffic
    G->>S: Finish mTLS and send HTTP request
    S-->>G: HTTP response
    G-->>W: HTTP response
    end
